<title>TURKEY: Turk Tofas 1996 net profits rise 42 pct.</title>
<headline>Turk Tofas 1996 net profits rise 42 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996 final results</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira)     545.11  vs    671.63</p>
<p>    Net profit		    4,578.96  vs  3,223.83</p>
<p>    Net sales		    63,400.09  vs 41,597.67</p>
<p>    Operating profit	    4,433.17  vs  3,226.49</p>
<p>    Exceptional income	  5,293.28  vs  3,019.70</p>
<p>    Interest Paid		 2,225.92  vs  1,356.57</p>
<p>    Total debts		  15,016.19  vs 12,456.26</p>
<p>    Equity			 24,344.97  vs 15,983.52</p>
<p>    Capital			 8,400.00  vs  4,800.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Leading Turkish car producer Tofas Turk Otomobil Fabrikalari A.S. is owned by Fiat Auto and Koc Holding, each holding a 37.86 percent stake.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 84.9 percent wholesale inflation in 1996.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul Newsroom +90-212-2750875</p>
</text>
